{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_mcp_uso_mcp_editor", "label": "MCP del editor (video-yt)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP_USO.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Va montado en el mismo backend FastAPI en vez de ser un proceso aparte, para que la IA y el usuario operen el mismo editor vivo (mismos proyectos, jobs y timeline)."}, {"id": "docs_mcp_uso_endpoint_streamable_http", "label": "Endpoint http://127.0.0.1:8000/mcp (streamable-HTTP)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP_USO.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_mcp_uso_backend_fastapi", "label": "Backend FastAPI (app.main:app v\u00eda uvicorn)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP_USO.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "El MCP solo existe si el backend est\u00e1 levantado; al arrancar, el log de diagn\u00f3stico indica el motor (GPU/CPU) y el encoder efectivo."}, {"id": "docs_mcp_uso_puente_mcp_remote", "label": "Puente mcp-remote para Claude Desktop", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP_USO.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Claude Desktop solo configura procesos stdio, as\u00ed que un MCP HTTP requiere el puente npx mcp-remote; Claude Code s\u00ed soporta transporte HTTP nativo."}, {"id": "docs_mcp_uso_catalogo_tools", "label": "Cat\u00e1logo de 50 tools (14 read / 33 write / 3 destructive)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP_USO.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_mcp_uso_niveles_politica", "label": "Niveles de pol\u00edtica (read / write / destructive)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP_USO.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Cada tool declara su nivel y a\u00f1ade meta.domain y annotations (read-only / destructive hints) para que el cliente pueda decidir qu\u00e9 requiere confirmaci\u00f3n."}, {"id": "docs_mcp_uso_auditoria_jsonl", "label": "Auditor\u00eda en backend/data/mcp_audit.jsonl", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP_USO.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Se registran tool, nivel, proyecto, claves de params \u2014nunca los valores\u2014 estado y ms, para poder auditar la actividad del modelo sin filtrar datos sensibles."}, {"id": "docs_mcp_uso_errores_estructurados", "label": "Errores estructurados (8 c\u00f3digos)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP_USO.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Un fallo devuelve is_error con {error:{code,message,retryable,param?,hint?}} y un enum cerrado (invalid_parameter, resource_not_found, operation_not_allowed, configuration_error, dependency_error, processing_error, temporary_error, job_running) para que el modelo pueda decidir si reintentar."}, {"id": "docs_mcp_uso_describe_capabilities", "label": "describe_capabilities(domain?)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP_USO.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Mueve los valores v\u00e1lidos (modelos, voces, motions, crop_modes) fuera del contexto de arranque: sin domain devuelve el mapa de dominios, con domain la gu\u00eda concreta bajo demanda."}, {"id": "docs_mcp_uso_list_projects", "label": "list_projects()", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP_USO.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_mcp_uso_resolve_project", "label": "resolve_project(query)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP_USO.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Resuelve por id/prefijo o nombre y devuelve candidates[] cuando es ambiguo en lugar de adivinar; el project_id resultante es obligatorio en el resto de tools."}, {"id": "docs_mcp_uso_resources", "label": "Resources de solo lectura (capabilities:// config:// help:// project://)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP_USO.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_mcp_uso_get_project_context", "label": "get_project_context(project_id)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP_USO.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Primer paso recomendado para orientarse: resume formato, material, timeline e historial en una sola llamada."}, {"id": "docs_mcp_uso_get_frame", "label": "get_frame(clip_id, at) \u2014 ojos de la IA", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP_USO.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Extrae un frame para que el modelo pueda mirar el v\u00eddeo, no solo leer metadatos."}, {"id": "docs_mcp_uso_search_transcript", "label": "search_transcript(query)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP_USO.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Permite editar por contenido buscando en el guion en lugar de por tiempos."}, {"id": "docs_mcp_uso_analyze_youtube", "label": "analyze_youtube(url) \u2014 tramos del heatmap", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP_USO.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_mcp_uso_create_clips_from_segments", "label": "create_clips_from_segments(project_id, url, segments, crop_mode)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP_USO.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_mcp_uso_add_to_timeline", "label": "add_to_timeline(project_id, kind, index)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP_USO.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_mcp_uso_reframe_clip", "label": "reframe_clip (center / manual)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP_USO.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_mcp_uso_set_project_format", "label": "set_project_format(aspect)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP_USO.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_mcp_uso_update_clip", "label": "update_clip(clip_id, patch)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP_USO.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Consolida los escalares (opacity, speed/keep_pitch/reverse, appear/exit, position/start/duration, role) en una sola operaci\u00f3n para que el cambio sea un \u00fanico undo."}, {"id": "docs_mcp_uso_set_clip_keyframes", "label": "set_clip_keyframes(x/y/scale/rotation/opacity)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP_USO.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_mcp_uso_animate_clip", "label": "animate_clip (zoom / giro / slide / aparecer con SFX)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP_USO.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "V\u00eda recomendada para animar: el modelo no debe escribir keyframes a mano, porque la tool garantiza curvas coherentes con el preview."}, {"id": "docs_mcp_uso_add_subtitles", "label": "add_subtitles(source_clip_id, segments)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP_USO.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_mcp_uso_transcribe", "label": "transcribe(project_id, source|clip_index, model?)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP_USO.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "El par\u00e1metro model es opcional; si se omite se usa el configurado en Ajustes (transcribe_settings), evitando que el modelo tenga que conocer la configuraci\u00f3n del usuario."}, {"id": "docs_mcp_uso_generate_voice", "label": "generate_voice(text, engine=kokoro|piper|gemini)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP_USO.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "El motor gemini requiere API key configurada; si falta, la tool lo comunica expl\u00edcitamente en lugar de fallar de forma opaca."}, {"id": "docs_mcp_uso_export_project", "label": "export_project(project_id)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP_USO.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_mcp_uso_jobs_wait_for_job", "label": "Jobs as\u00edncronos y wait_for_job(job_id, timeout_s)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP_USO.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Recorte, transcripci\u00f3n y export devuelven {id, status} en vez de bloquear; el cliente espera con wait_for_job y puede cancelar con cancel_job."}, {"id": "docs_mcp_uso_undo_redo_checkpoints", "label": "undo / redo / checkpoint / restore_checkpoint", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP_USO.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_mcp_uso_edicion_transaccional", "label": "Edici\u00f3n transaccional (snapshot \u2192 aplicar \u2192 validar \u2192 guardar)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/MCP_USO.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Toda edici\u00f3n del MCP es transaccional y deshacible porque el modelo escribe sobre el mismo proyecto vivo que el usuario est\u00e1 editando."}, {"id": "docs_mcp_uso_gpu_autodeteccion", "label": "Auto-detecci\u00f3n de GPU (whisper CUDA + FFmpeg NVENC)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP_USO.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Se sondea NVENC de verdad antes de usarlo y se puede forzar CPU con VIDEOYT_GPU=0; en la m\u00e1quina actual NVENC est\u00e1 bloqueado por un driver NVIDIA viejo."}, {"id": "docs_mcp_uso_flujo_a_youtube_short", "label": "Flujo A \u2014 create_short_from_youtube (autom\u00e1tico)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP_USO.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_mcp_uso_flujo_b_biblioteca", "label": "Flujo B \u2014 make_short_from_library", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP_USO.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_mcp_uso_flujo_c_pilotaje_manual", "label": "Flujo C \u2014 pilotaje manual (control total)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/MCP_USO.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Existe junto a los workflows de una sola llamada para casos donde se quiere control paso a paso; si algo 